# Go API Rules

## Layout

```
api/
├── cmd/server/main.go       # wiring + router.Register
├── cmd/migrate/main.go      # standalone AutoMigrate
├── internal/
│   ├── router/              # Route registration by context
│   │   ├── router.go        # Register(app, Deps)
│   │   ├── health.go        # /v1/health
│   │   ├── auth.go          # /v1/auth/login, verify
│   │   └── user.go          # /v1/auth/register
│   ├── handler/             # One subpackage per domain
│   │   ├── auth/
│   │   ├── user/
│   │   ├── health/
│   │   └── httperr/         # Shared error mapping
│   ├── service/             # auth/, user/ + shared.go
│   ├── middleware/
│   ├── email/
│   ├── database/            # Open, WithTx, Ping
│   ├── model/               # GORM models
│   └── repository/          # data access layer
```

## Standards

- Go 1.25+, Fiber v2 for HTTP
- All API routes under `/v1` prefix
- PostgreSQL via GORM + repository layer — services never use `*gorm.DB` directly
- Schema via GORM AutoMigrate in `database.Open`
- Register new routes in `internal/router/{context}.go`, not in `main.go`
- Map errors via `httperr.Write(c, err)` in handlers

## Adding an endpoint

1. Add GORM model in `internal/model/` (if new table)
2. Add repository methods in `internal/repository/`
3. Add service method in `internal/service/{context}/`
4. Add handler method in `internal/handler/{context}/`
5. Register route in `internal/router/{context}.go`
6. Add tests

## Secrets

- Never return decrypted secret values in list endpoints
- Redact secret values in structured logs
- OTP codes logged only in development
